AB  - .Although coupled Th-230/U-234-ESR analyses have become routine for dating teeth, they have never been used for corals. While the ESR age depends on, and requires assumptions about, the time-averaged cosmic dose rate, (D) over bar (cos)(t), Th-230/U-234 dates do not. Since (D) over bar (cos)(t) received by corals depends on the attenuation by any intervening material, (D) over bar (cos)(t) response reflects changing water depths and sediment cover. By coupling the two methods, one can determine the age and a unique (D) over bar (cos,coupled)(t) simultaneously. From a coral's water depth and sedimentary history as predicted by a given sealevel curve, one can predict (D) over bar (cos,sealevel)(t)- If (D) over bar (cos,coupled) (t) agrees well with (D) over bar (cos,sealevel)(t), this provides independent validation for the curve used to build (D) over bar (cos,sealevel)(t). For six corals dated at 7-128ka from Florida Platform reef crests, the sealevel curve by Waelbroeck et al. [2002. Sea-level and deep water temperature changes derived from benthonic foraminifera isotopic records. Quat. Sci. Rev. 21, 295-305] predicted their (D) over bar (cos,coupled)(t) values as well as, or better than, the SPECMAP sealevel curve. Where a whole reef can be sampled over a transect, a precise test for sealevel curves could be developed. (c) 2007 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.
