AB  - Fiji beset by a host of development-related environmental problems. The most serious involve the degradation of coastal areas, especially mangroves, and the destruction of coral reefs. Land reclamation to grow sugar cane and rice on the 2 main islands of Viti Levu and Vanua Levu were responsible for most of the loss of mangrove forests. And the islands'' coral reefs are being smothered by increasing loads of sediment (mostly from poorly planned and executed development projects) transported into the coastal zones by river and streams. Fiji needs a coastal zone management plan and the resources to carry it out.
