AB  - Laboratory tests were made of the responses and resistance of 23 species and varieties of reef corals to such environmental factors as high and low temp., salinity, sunlight, and silt deposit. Results of these tests are compared with the conditions under which the various coral spp. occur in nature. The 2 spp. most resistant to extremes of the factors tested are Favia hawaiiensis and Leptas-trea agassizi. Seaweeds are especially destructive of coral colonies owing to their smothering effect.
